# PUBG Shorts — Template KS1 (Kill Shots)

Use when the user asks for **KS1**, "kill shots", or knock/kill-only cuts.

Follow **global GPU/thermal hard rules** — never batch-OCR whole matches; detect banner flashes on GPU crops, OCR only sparse candidates.

## Include
- Moments where **I knocked** an enemy
- Moments where **I killed / finished** an enemy
- Keep knock→finish as one sequence when close together

## Exclude (KS1-specific)
- Chicken Dinner / winner screen (even if present)
- Final-circle atmosphere without a knock/kill
- Utility throws, looting, rotations, zone pressure **unless** they sit inside the kill-shot padding window
- Spectator / death-cam / watching teammates
- Other players' kills in the feed that are not mine

## Detection priority
1. Center tip: `YOU KNOCKED OUT` / `YOU KILLED` (tolerate OCR garble)
2. Kill feed / match log: `[ASA] rkanik` on the **left** (killer) with knock (X/crawl) or kill icon — not when rkanik is the victim on the right
3. Skip spectator POV (highlighted teammate that isn't me)
4. Never rely only on clean OCR — feed lines like `rkanik [AUG] X enemy` count as my knock

## Pacing
- Padding: 4s before / 3s after each knock or kill (global defaults)
- Hard cuts between separate fights
- Target ~45–90s; keep every confirmed knock/kill even if longer
- No CD end-card; end on the last kill-shot

## Title / tags
- Moment type: kill montage / multi kill / knock chain — **not** chicken dinner
- Omit `#ChickenDinner` unless a different template confirms a win
